note E14 stack rule (positive): a callee writes a secret byte through a pointer to the caller's local array.
note The array lies below the entry SP, so it cannot be the declared count field. With e14 the store is
note excused (stack-below-entry-sp) and the count load stays public. Without e14 the pointer is unknown.
fn fill t edit uchar 8 a view uchar 1 to ulong
put t 3 get a 0
ret 0
end
fn f c view uchar 104 a view uchar 1 to ulong
t = new uchar 8 0
s = fill t a
if eq ulong get c 32 s
ret 0
end
ret 1
end
